provider: ollama-cloud (glm-5.3)
request: In the watchlist, show movies I haven't watched yet before the ones I've watched.

governor turn 1: plan -> watchlist  (Unwatched-first ordering is a display concern of the watchlist view, so the change is contained in the watchlist unit: derive its existing public `movies` signal as a stable, unwatched-first computed over `store.items()` and render from it. The store's persisted order and all other consumers (search, movie-detail, app) are untouched, so no interface changes are needed.)
round 1: owners watchlist=rejected; oracle RED
governor turn 2: plan -> watchlist  (Last round was rejected only because the watchlist owner edited two existing tests without approval; the implementation itself was on target, and since nothing was applied the acceptance test still fails (unwatched-first order not implemented). Both test edits are legitimate consequences of the request: their index-based re-query of the first row's checkbox assumed a toggled movie stays in place, which the new ordering intentionally changes, and the edits preserve the tests' intent while remaining order-agnostic. I therefore approve those two test changes and re-issue the same watchlist-only plan.)
round 2: owners watchlist=ok; oracle GREEN
!! GOVERNOR ISOLATION LEAK: 1 source line(s) in governor prompt
governor turn 3: accept  (The watchlist now renders unwatched movies before watched ones: the owner made `movies` a stable, unwatched-first sort of the store's items (without mutating the store), the template renders from `movies()`, and the two approved test edits adapted index-based queries to the new ordering. Oracle is green (tsc exit 0, 30 tests passed), and the acceptance test confirms both the component signal ordering and the on-screen order.)

